# Commits `git blame` should skip: whole-tree reformats and other
# mechanical, no-behaviour-change diffs, so a blame on a line inside one
# still surfaces the commit that last changed its content, not the
# commit that merely reflowed it.
#
# Use it with:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
# (per-clone, not committed to any git config -- this file is the shared
# part, the `git config` line is each developer's own opt-in) or, for a
# one-off:
#   git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs <path>
#
# GitHub's own blame view reads this file automatically, with no config
# needed on either side, if it sits at the repository root under this
# exact name.
#
# Squash-merging (this repository's only merge method -- DEVELOPER-AGENTS.md's
# "Merging") means the commit a PR branch lands as on `main` is one GitHub
# composes at merge time, so its SHA cannot be known before the merge and
# so cannot be recorded in the same PR that creates it. Each entry below
# lands in a small follow-up PR instead, immediately after the reformat it
# names merges, and the two are described together in that follow-up's
# body rather than split silently.

